# Intent: A frame recorder for the grid games' animations on bench images, because a serial snapshot takes seconds and a disc drops in a few hundred milliseconds. self.game.bench_record starts or stops recording one sample per 30 ms game tick (up to 4.8 s) and self.game.bench_frames returns the rows [t_ms, tweens running, top of the highest falling disc, narrowest flipping card in permille, flags] with the biggest gap between two ticks, so the drop, the bounce, the pulses, the shake and the card flip can be checked after the fact. self.game.bench_tap now reaches the grid games too (it answered "No game is running" for them).
# Placement: unit (bench only)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.game.start connect4, self.game.bench_record {on 1}, self.game.bench_tap x 60 y 120, wait 2 s, self.game.bench_frames: the fall_y column rises monotonically with growing steps, shows the bounce (a few values back up by up to 8 px), the unit's reply falls after the person's landing, and gaps_ms stays near 30; with match the flip column goes from 1000 to 0 and back.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_GAMES_BENCH (bench images only)
# Memory cost: about 2 KB of static memory in bench images only (160 samples of 8 bytes plus code); none in the plain image.

